```

Wait — the new test expects `result['success'] == true` when the poster throws. Note `_postTraceComment` is awaited in the run loop (`await _postTraceComment(key)`); a throw would propagate and fail the job (unhandled). Java catches per ticket and continues. Adding try/catch around ALL trace comments (Jira too) — Java does exactly that (try/catch around postComment, warn + continue). Good — Java parity for both backends.

And the github default poster:

```dart
Future<void> _githubCommentPoster(String key, String body) async {
  GithubTrackerClient().postComment(key, body);
}
```

postComment returns void and throws StateError on failure — wrapped by the try/catch above. 

